# Run sections in walkthrough order. Change ports here if you changed .env.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8180
@instance = getting-started-server
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/instances/{{instance}}
@locations = http://127.0.0.1:8182/sources/location-tracker/events

### Exact runtime readiness
GET {{api}}/runtime

### Source status
GET {{api}}/sources/my-postgres

### Step 3: first result set
GET {{api}}/queries/all-messages/results

### Step 4: consume the all-messages query output
POST {{api}}/queries
Content-Type: application/json

< ./configs/hello-world-senders.json

### Replace the Log reaction to subscribe to both queries
PUT {{api}}/reactions/log-reaction
Content-Type: application/json

{"kind":"log","id":"log-reaction","queries":["all-messages","hello-world-senders"],"autoStart":true}

### Filtered result set
GET {{api}}/queries/hello-world-senders/results

### Step 5: aggregation
POST {{api}}/queries
Content-Type: application/json

< ./configs/message-counts.json

### Aggregated result set
GET {{api}}/queries/message-counts/results

### Step 6: source-based change timestamps
POST {{api}}/queries
Content-Type: application/json

< ./configs/inactive-senders.json

### Inactive senders
GET {{api}}/queries/inactive-senders/results

### Step 7: locations source (relative to Server's .runtime/<run-id> working directory)
POST {{api}}/sources
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind":"http", "id":"location-tracker", "autoStart":true,
  "host":"127.0.0.1", "port":8182,
  "bootstrapProvider":{"kind":"scriptfile","filePaths":["../../locations.jsonl"]}
}

### Join the query output with location data
POST {{api}}/queries
Content-Type: application/json

< ./configs/messages-with-location.json

### Joined current result set
GET {{api}}/queries/messages-with-location/results

### Move Brian
POST {{locations}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"operation":"update","element":{"type":"node","id":"brian","labels":["UserLocation"],"properties":{"name":"Brian Kernighan","location":"Conference Room B","status":"away"}}}

### After inserting Carol's message in PostgreSQL, add her location
POST {{locations}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"operation":"insert","element":{"type":"node","id":"carol","labels":["UserLocation"],"properties":{"name":"Carol","location":"Home Office","status":"online"}}}

### List reactions (confirm the CLI removes its own temporary reaction on exit)
GET {{api}}/reactions
